::Data vs Information::
In computer processing, what is the key distinction between data and information?
[difficulty:medium]
[chapter:Fundamentals of Computer]
[tags:data,information]
{
    =Data refers to raw facts and figures that do not make much sense on their own, while information is the processed, meaningful results
    ~Data is the final output printed on paper, while information is the raw keyboard input entered by the user
    ~Data can only represent numbers, while information represents text, audio, and video formats
    ~Data is stored in primary memory (RAM), while information is stored exclusively in secondary memory (HDD)
}

