[chapter:Data Representation and Processing]
[tags:data,digital]
{
    =Information represented and stored in a digital format consisting of discrete binary values (0 and 1)
    ~Information represented in a physical quantity that varies continuously
    ~Information written in descriptive paragraphs of text
    ~Information collected exclusively through analog thermometers and clocks
}

::Analog vs Digital Clocks::
What represents an analog clock's data versus a digital clock's data?
[difficulty:medium]
[chapter:Data Representation and Processing]
[tags:data,comparison]
{
    =Analog clock data is continuous and varying; Digital clock data consists of discrete values representing digits
    ~Analog clock data is digital; Digital clock data is continuous
    ~Analog clocks represent binary values; Digital clocks represent infinite physical positions
    ~There is no technical difference in how their data is represented
}

